---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Privacy">
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <h2>Your workspace stays in this tab</h2>
  <p>
    The sender imports public keys and encrypts messages locally with native
    WebCrypto. After the static page and its local assets load, typing, key
    import, encryption, raw recovery and artwork exports make no application
    network requests. Private keys and their passphrases belong only in the
    separate offline receiver.
  </p>
  <p>
    There is no message history, autosave, account, analytics, remote font,
    tracking widget, error collector or service worker. Drafts, custom public
    keys, ciphertext and recovery inputs remain in memory. Clear everything,
    reload and leaving the workspace discard its state; returning through
    browser history resets it too. Encryption clears the draft after success.
  </p>
  <h2>What persists outside the application</h2>
  <p>
    Copy, download and print are explicit exports. Clipboard managers, saved
    ciphertext/artwork, print spools and PDFs can retain copies after this tab
    closes. The receiver deliberately saves authenticated plaintext to a new
    private local file; it does not keep an application history or automatically
    open an editor. You control who can access those files.
  </p>
  <p>
    The Windows receiver has opt-in <code>--cleanup-output</code> and
    <code>--single-use-key</code> options. They run a bounded seven-pass
    overwrite and handle-based deletion only after successful authentication,
    output flush/close and a local finish prompt. This is best effort, not
    guaranteed sanitization: when cleanup is requested, the receiver makes a
    best-effort check for Windows shadow-copy device names visible to the
    process. The check may miss snapshots and does not establish their absence;
    it cannot verify backups, sync copies, paging, SSD remapping, OS copies or
    copies outside its selected paths. Static private keys are preserved unless
    the user explicitly marks that key file single-use.
  </p>
  <p>
    Owned temporary byte buffers are cleared where possible. JavaScript strings,
    browser undo/restoration buffers, extensions, keyboards, the operating
    system and garbage collection cannot provide guaranteed secure erasure.
    Clearing the page does not wipe exported files or the clipboard.
  </p>
  <h2>Static hosting and delivered code</h2>
  <p>
    Loading a hosted page sends ordinary IP, path and browser metadata to its
    hosting provider; static access logs and normal asset caching may exist.
    Browser or operating-system traffic is outside this application's control.
    Reloading a hosted page while offline is not promised.
  </p>
  <p>
    These properties describe the intended build. A compromised host, extension
    or device can capture plaintext or replace the recipient key. Before typing
    sensitive content when you do not trust the host, use a reviewed local
    sender whose complete file was verified through an independent trusted
    channel. No reviewed release is available yet. Read the
    <a href="/security/">security and verification guidance</a>.
  </p>
</Layout>
